      "content": "thanks for the methods suggestion. looking closer at the data, the correlation between the increase in Hispanic and Black populations and the larceny spike is really strong, almost too strong to ignore in the feature engineering phase. when i'm setting up the weights in the random forest, should i treat the ethnic composition quintiles as a primary driver for the risk score? i want to make sure the model is being 'realistic' about the local community dynamics so it doesn't under-predict the risk in these specific areas.",
